## Context

Optional follow-up. Core UUID lifecycle and basic applicability already belong to 0911/0921. No broad grammar is needed before the travelling project works.

Design baseline: v7. v6 was merged by PR #903 and is frozen at `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-v6.md`; v7 closes the acceptance review's four §12.1 conditions and settles the nomenclature, leaving the architecture and this ticket's scope unchanged. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`, `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-nomenclature.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Library predicate interface; actual adapter misses; `docs/2026-09-10-valid-while-coverage-ledger.md`.

## Actions

1. Identify an observed scope/filtering failure requiring a new operator before implementing it.
2. Add a bounded closed-grammar operator with explicit roots, costs and false/unknown semantics; never execute memory-authored shell.
3. Keep unknown distinct from true. Retraction/supersession cannot revive when an environmental predicate changes.
4. Record the operator decision and consumer evidence; retain no-change/deferred if there is no demonstrated need.

## Test

Operator fixtures cover true, false, unknown, malformed input and resource bounds in a relocated checkout. An inactive body remains inactive even when the condition becomes true.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v7, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Any extension justified by a concrete consumer failure and validated offline.
- [ ] No slug supersedes field, universal write-time truth requirement or automatic lifecycle revival.
- [ ] Not a prerequisite for core completion.
